.Fl V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
serves the
.Ql arcana
cblink family: it reports the jails of this host and changes them for
clients such as the arcana web console and
.Xr arcanactl 8 .
It is the only privileged part of arcana.
.Pp
Running jails are read with
.Xr jail_getv 3
and their processes with
.Xr libprocstat 3 .
Configured jails are read with
.Ql jail -f file -e
for
.Pa /etc/jail.conf
and every
.Pa /etc/jail.conf.d/*.conf
that
.Pa /etc/jail.conf
does not include, the files
.Pa /etc/rc.d/jail
would use, so variables, includes and shared statements mean what they
mean to
.Xr jail 8 .
.Pp
Starting, stopping and restarting run
.Xr jail 8
with
.Fl c ,
.Fl r
or
.Fl rc
and the file that defines the jail, so the jail's
.Va exec.*
hooks, mounts and interfaces are handled as usual.
Killing removes the jail with
.Xr jail_remove 2 .
Addresses change in the running jail with
.Xr jail_setv 3
and, when the jail has an
.Va interface ,
an alias added or removed on it; in the configuration they change in
place with libjailconf, as
.Xr jailconf 8
does.
The previous file is kept as
.Pa file.arcana.bak ,
and if
.Xr jail 8
does not read the new file as intended it is put back.
.Pp
Beyond jails it reports and changes the host itself, always through the
system's own programs.
Services are the executable scripts of
.Pa /etc/rc.d
and
.Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d :
whether they are enabled is read from
.Ql sysrc -A ,
whether the enabled ones run from
.Ql service name status ;
they are started, stopped, restarted and reloaded with
.Xr service 8
(arcana-services' actions, its
.Ic read
the one service's state); enabled and disabled, and their
.Xr rc.conf 5
variables set, by a commit of arcana-services
.Pq Sx CONFIGURATION ,
or by a job with
.Xr sysrc 8 .
The routing table, the nexthops, the active connections and the open
sockets are what
.Xr netstat 1
and
.Xr sockstat 1
print with
.Fl -libxo Cm json ,
one run per address family.
Usage figures are the CPU share from
.Va kern.cp_time
between two requests, memory from the
.Va vm.stats.vm
counters, swap from
.Xr swapinfo 8
and the ZFS pools from
.Xr zpool 8 :
arcana-host's
.Ic host ,
with what
.Xr uname 3
and the sysctls say of the host, read when asked and nothing else with
it.
The certificates OpenSSL trusts, of the host or of a jail, are its
.Ic read-certificates
action: each of
.Pa /etc/ssl/certs
and
.Pa /etc/ssl/untrusted
read with OpenSSL, which no read of the host waits for.
Packages that the repository has newer versions of are listed with
.Ql pkg version -vRl '<'
and upgraded with
.Ql pkg upgrade -y ,
on the host or, with
.Ql pkg -j ,
in a running jail.
What runs is arcana-processes' list, read with
.Va kern.proc.proc
twice for the CPU shares between the looks; one process's files and
threads its
.Ic read
action, with
.Xr libprocstat 3 .
A log is read by arcana-log's
.Ic read
action, of the log directory or a jail's own, the files there with
it.
How busy the host has been is arcana-history's
.Ic read ,
the samples after a time with how they are taken; how it samples and
its limits are arcana-history's configuration, a commit of it written
to its history file
.Pq Fl 1 .
What happened on the host is arcana-events'
.Ic read ,
the events after a number, and its
.Ic event
notification, each as it happens.
Packets are followed through the firewall by arcana-firewall's
.Ic trace ,
the kernel's
.Ql ipfw:::rule-matched
probe told to
.Xr dtrace 1 ;
what the host does with a packet and its reply, nothing sent, by
arcana-troubleshoot's
.Ic path-check ,
one round of
.Xr traceroute 8
by its
.Ic traceroute ,
and packets taken with
.Xr tcpdump 1
by its
.Ic capture
(without an interface, the sources there are).
.Pp
Every reply carries a trace: the library calls, system calls, files and
programs the request used, with the output of every program.
Changes are made one at a time; reading is not held up by them.
Jobs of pkg in jails are the exception: those at the head of the queue,
each in a jail of its own, run up to four at once, a jail's own one
after another, so that a download stalled in one jail holds up no
other; the next job of any other kind waits for all of them.
Such a job can be cancelled while it runs: its pkg is stopped.
.Pp
Every operation requires an authenticated peer.
On a local socket that is anyone who can open it: the socket is mode
0600, or 0660 with
.Fl g .
On the network it is a peer with a client certificate issued by
.Ar cafile ,
over TLS 1.3.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl A Ar cafile
Certificate authority for client certificates.
.It Fl C Ar certfile , Fl K Ar keyfile
This server's certificate and key.
The three files are read at startup, before the daemon detaches: one
that is missing, unreadable, not PEM, or a key that is not the
certificate's, is an error that names the file.
.It Fl D Ar confdir
Per-jail configuration files: where a commit of arcana-jails puts a
jail new, a file of its own,
.Ar name Ns .conf .
Default
.Pa /etc/jail.conf.d .
Its files, with the one of
.Fl f
and the templates, are arcana-jail-files'
.Ic read-files
action on the jails, read when asked: no read of the jails waits for
them.
.It Fl d
Log debugging messages.
.It Fl F
Stay in the foreground and log to standard error.
.It Fl f Ar jail.conf
Main configuration file.
With the files of
.Fl D ,
arcana-jails' running datastore: each jail's parameters as
.Xr jail 8
.Fl e
resolves them, which a commit writes in the jail's own block, in
place, every other line kept, read back by
.Xr jail 8
before it stands; and whether rc.d/jail starts it,
.Va jail_list
and
.Va jail_enable
in Arcana's rc.conf file.
Default
.Pa /etc/jail.conf .
.It Fl g Ar group
Make local sockets mode 0660 and owned by
.Ar group .
.It Fl j Ar jail
The
.Xr jail 8
program.
.It Fl l Ar uri
Listen on
.Ar uri ,
which may be given up to eight times:
.Ql unix:/path ,
.Ql tcp://address:port
or
.Ql sctp://address[,address ...]:port .
Network listeners need
.Fl A ,
.Fl C
and
.Fl K .
Default
.Ql unix:/var/run/arcana-agent.sock .
Beside every
.Ql tcp://
listener
.Nm
listens on SCTP at the same address and port, where the kernel has
SCTP.
It does not load the
.Xr sctp 4
module, and where it is missing does not try again by itself: it is
told to with arcana-agent's
.Ic retry
action of its
.Ic transport ,
as
.Xr arcanactl 8
.Cm transport retry
does.
The listeners, the connections open and each SCTP association's paths
are that container's state; its
.Ic listen
action listens on another address, closes one and keeps the change in
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
.It Fl p Ar pidfile
Default
.Pa /var/run/arcana-agent.pid .
.It Fl R Ar rc.d dirs
The directories whose scripts are the host's services, colon separated.
Default
.Pa /etc/rc.d:/usr/local/etc/rc.d .
.It Fl s Ar service
The
.Xr service 8
program, which lists, queries and changes services.
.It Fl y Ar sysrc
The
.Xr sysrc 8
program, which reads and writes their
.Xr rc.conf 5
variables.
.It Fl U Ar program
The file an update replaces.
The default is the running program.
.It Fl B Ar dir
Where a tree is cloned and built.
Default
.Pa /var/cache/arcana-build .
.It Fl c Ar config.mk
This host's settings for a build, copied into the tree when the file
exists.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana/config.mk .
.It Fl G Ar git , Fl M Ar make
The
.Xr git 1
and
.Xr make 1
programs.
.It Fl X Ar traceroute
The
.Xr traceroute 8
program; for IPv6 the same name with
.Ql 6
after it,
.Xr traceroute6 8 .
Default
.Pa /usr/sbin/traceroute .
.It Fl V
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl w Ar seconds
How long a change made in safe mode waits to be confirmed (a job's; a
commit's is the commit's own).
Default 60.
.It Fl -sctp-also Ar addresses
More addresses, separated by spaces, that every SCTP listener is bound
to beside its own
.Pq Xr sctp_bindx 3 :
an association with the console has a path to each, and goes on over
another when one fails.
An IPv4 listener takes IPv4 addresses, an IPv6 one either.
What cannot be bound is said with the listener in arcana-agent's
.Ic transport ,
and the addresses are changed by its
.Ic listen
action while the agent runs
.Pq kept in rc.conf as arcana_agent_sctp_also .
.It Fl -telegram-api Ar url
Where the Telegram Bot API is, for the notify operation.
Default
.Pa https://api.telegram.org ;
a test's own server otherwise.
.It Fl -poudriere Ar poudriere
.Xr poudriere 8 ,
the package builder, a plugin of the host's.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/bin/poudriere .
The builder operation reads its build jails, ports trees, make.conf
files, options directories, package repositories and latest builds
(each with its failed ports and the end of their logs) where poudriere
keeps them; builder-options reads a port's options with
.Ql make showconfig ,
run as
.Fl M Ns 's
.Xr make 1 ;
the poudriere job makes, updates and deletes jails and trees, sets a
port's options and builds ports.
A jail or tree made or updated, and a build, take longer than a job
should hold the queue: the job starts poudriere under a waiter of its
own and ends, the run going on after it
.Pq and after the agent's restart ;
its output, pid and exit status are kept as
.Pa builder/ Ns Ar n Ns Pa .log ,
.Pa .pid
and
.Pa .exit
beside the history configuration, the last 20 runs.
A run is stopped as a terminal would stop it, SIGINT to its process
group.
.It Fl -poudriere-etc Ar directory
Where
.Pa poudriere.conf
and
.Pa poudriere.d
are.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc .
.It Fl -rtadvctl Ar rtadvctl
The
.Xr rtadvctl 8
run to reload
.Xr rtadvd 8
after a commit of an interface's router advertisements, and to read
what it sends for the operational datastore
.Pq Cm show .
Default
.Pa /usr/sbin/rtadvctl .
.It Fl -pkg-idle Ar seconds
How long
.Xr pkg 8
may say nothing before it is stopped, with what it started
.Pq Nm pkg Fl j Ns 's child in the jail :
a download that stalls, or a question pkg waits on.
Off a terminal pkg prints a dot for each tenth of a download.
Default 600.
.It Fl -jobs-conf Ar file
Where how many jobs of pkg in jails run at once is kept
.Pq arcana-jobs' Li lanes , written by a commit ;
.Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana/jobs.conf
by default.
.It Fl -nacm Ar file
Where the access rules are kept: ietf-netconf-acm's nacm (RFC 8341), as
YANG-CBOR, written whole by an EDIT of it;
.Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana/nacm.cbor
by default.
Without it, the console's admin and the console are in group admin,
which may do anything, and anyone else may read and ask but change
nothing; a command that changes the host is run only by a rule that
permits it.
Root on the unix socket is the recovery session, which no rule holds
back; another local account is
.Li local: Ns Ar login
to the rules, never one of the console's users.
An rpc or action of Arcana's modules that changes the host is
.Ic nacm:default-deny-all :
run only by a rule that permits it.
.It Fl -features Ar list
Of the features
.Ic hello
names, what this agent takes that one before it did not, only those in
.Ar list ,
separated by commas; one left out is refused as an agent before it
refuses it.
All of them by default.
It stands in for an older agent, for a test of what a client sends one.
The only feature is
.Li gzip-update :
a program for
.Cm agent-update
compressed, and
.Cm agent-build Ns 's
sent back so.
.It Fl -subscriptions Ar file
Where the configured subscriptions are kept (RFC 8639 section 2.5):
ietf-subscribed-notifications' subscriptions container, as YANG-CBOR,
written whole by a commit;
.Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana/subscriptions.cbor
by default.
Each subscription's receivers name a receiver instance
(ietf-subscribed-notif-receivers), an https-receiver
(ietf-https-notif-transport) with its capabilities-endpoint and
relay-notification-endpoint, both
.Li https://host[:port]/path :
the agent reads the capabilities once, which must take JSON, then
POSTs each record as RFC 8040's notification JSON, over HTTP/1.1 on one
TLS connection kept open, showing the certificate of
.Fl C
and
.Fl K
and trusting the CA of
.Fl A
and the system's.
An https-receiver with a token (arcana-notif's
.Li token
leaf) sends it with each request as
.Li Authorization: Bearer ;
it is kept with the container, which the file holds at mode 0600, and
is
.Ic nacm:default-deny-all :
read or written by a rule that permits it, or the recovery session.
A receiver that fails is connected again, a second on and doubling to
a minute, told subscription-started with the time of the last record
it had, and sent what it missed from the events kept (configured-replay)
then replay-completed.
The console is the receiver meant: its
.Pa /api/servers/<host>/subscription
says what to put in the candidate, and
.Pa /api/servers/<host>/subscription/token
hands the host a token in it, for a console that knows its hosts by
their tokens (web.conf's notif_auth) rather than their certificates.
.It Fl -bird-watch Ar seconds
How often the BIRD of the host, and that of each running jail with a
network of its own where
.Xr birdc 8
is, are read for faults: a BGP session turned on but not established
.Pq Ql bgp-neighbor ,
an OSPF neighbour that was full and is no more
.Pq Ql ospf-neighbor ,
a BFD session that was up and is down
.Pq Ql bfd ,
a BIRD that answered and does not
.Pq Ql bird-instance .
Each is cleared when it is well again, and is an
.Ql sdwan-fault
event too.
Default 15; 0 reads them never.
A program the kernel saw die of a signal that dumps core
.Pq Va kern.logsigexit
is a fault whatever the value,
.Ql crash ,
Major, of
.Ql host:bird
or
.Ql jail:web/nginx :
the signal by name, how many times in 24 hours, and why there is no
core when there is none
.Po a daemon that set its group, as
.Nm bird Fl g
does, dumps none while
.Va kern.sugid_coredump
is 0
.Pc ;
said anew at each crash, cleared after an hour without one.
.It Fl -smtpd-watch Ar seconds
How often OpenSMTPD is looked at, on the host and in each running jail
where
.Xr smtpd 8
is: its counters
.Pq Ql smtpctl show stats
kept, a day of them, for the Mail tab's graphs, and a
.Ql mail
fault when it is enabled and not running, or when more are queued than
the limit the tab set
.Pq Pa watch.json No beside its tables .
Default 60; 0 looks never.
.It Fl I Ar ifconfig , Fl n Ar ngctl , Fl k Ar wg , Fl b Ar birdc
The
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
.Xr ngctl 8 ,
.Xr wg 8
and
.Xr birdc 8
programs.
.It Fl e Ar bird , Fl a Ar file
The
.Xr bird 8
program, which parses a configuration before it is put in place, and
BIRD's main configuration file.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/bird.conf .
.It Fl z Ar zfs , Fl q Ar gpart , Fl i Ar camcontrol , Fl m Ar mount , Fl u Ar umount
The programs storage is read and changed with:
.Xr zfs 8 ,
.Xr gpart 8 ,
.Xr camcontrol 8 ,
.Xr mount 8
and
.Xr umount 8 .
.Xr zpool 8
is
.Fl Z .
.It Fl S Ar fstab
The
.Xr fstab 5
read, and edited.
Default:
.Pa /etc/fstab .
.It Fl h Ar ipfw , Fl J Ar ipfw.rules
The
.Xr ipfw 8
program, and the file of its commands that holds the kept rules of the
firewall.
Default:
.Pa /sbin/ipfw
and
.Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana/ipfw.rules .
.It Fl Q Ar sysctl , Fl O Ar sysctl.conf
The
.Xr sysctl 8
program, which sets a variable of the kernel's state, and the
.Xr sysctl.conf 5
that keeps one for the next boot: arcana-sysctl's running datastore,
which a commit writes in place, every other line kept, and sets the
kernel to.
Default:
.Pa /sbin/sysctl
and
.Pa /etc/sysctl.conf
(under the root
.Fl -root
names, where given).
.It Fl v Ar log-directory
Where
.Xr syslogd 8
writes: the files a log is read from.
Default:
.Pa /var/log .
.It Fl 1 Ar history.conf
Where the agent keeps how it was told to sample the host: every how
many seconds, and how many samples it keeps.
Without the file, every five seconds and an hour of it.
Default:
.Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana/history.conf .
.It Fl 2 Ar directory
Where the programs are that have no option of their own:
.Xr newfs 8 ,
.Xr growfs 8 ,
.Xr fstyp 8 ,
.Xr swapon 8 ,
.Xr swapoff 8 ,
.Xr nvmecontrol 8
and
.Xr smartctl 8 .
Without it they are looked for where the system keeps such.
.It Fl T Ar kldload , Fl t Ar kldunload
The
.Xr kldload 8
and
.Xr kldunload 8
programs, which load a kernel module and unload one.
.It Fl x Ar jexec
The
.Xr jexec 8
program, which runs the jail's own programs in it.
Whether a jail runs with a network of its own, where its root is and
its release are read with
.Xr jail_getv 3 .
.It Fl H Ar helper
The program run to look at a jail's network from inside it: its
interfaces, its routes through
.Xr netlink 4 ,
its connections and sockets from the kernel's lists of them.
Default: this program itself, which then reads the host's own routes,
connections and sockets in the daemon, without running anything; and
which makes a
.Xr netlink 4
socket inside each jail with a network of its own and hands it over,
so that the daemon is told of that network's changes as of the
host's; and which serves, attached to each jail with a network of its
own, the models as the jail has them, its logical network element's
.Ic root
(RFC 8530, an inline mount of RFC 8528's): its interfaces, its
routing, its FIBs as network instances with their own
.Ic vrf-root ,
its YANG library.
One such helper runs for each jail read, from its first read until
the jail stops, and is started again where it died.
Another helper cannot: the jails' networks are then not watched, and
their elements have no root.
.It Fl o Ar directory
Where WireGuard interfaces are written for
.Xr wg-quick 8 .
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/wireguard .
.It Fl r Ar swanctl
strongSwan's
.Xr swanctl 8 ,
for IPsec: the
.Cm strongswan
plugin, there when it is.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/sbin/swanctl .
.It Fl 5 Ar directory
Where
.Xr swanctl 8
reads from: the host's own key is made in its
.Pa pkcs8
directory, mode 0600, and its public half written to
.Pa pubkey/arcana.pub ;
a connection is written to
.Pa conf.d/arcana- Ns Ar name Ns Pa .conf ,
IKEv2 only, with its peer's key in
.Pa pubkey .
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/swanctl .
.It Fl N Ar netstat
The
.Xr netstat 1
program, run with
.Fl -libxo Cm json
for the nexthops and the nexthop groups.
.It Fl W Ar swapinfo , Fl Z Ar zpool
The
.Xr swapinfo 8
and
.Xr zpool 8
programs, for the usage figures; a host without ZFS reports no pools.
.It Fl P Ar pkg
The
.Xr pkg 8
program, for pending upgrades and upgrading, on the host and with
.Fl j
in running jails: arcana-packages' state, its read, refresh and
upgrade actions, and the pkg jobs.
Upgrades may run for up to an hour, and are stopped sooner when pkg
says nothing for
.Fl -pkg-idle
seconds.
.El
.Pp
A program run for a read, and for the samples the history keeps, runs
at nice 10
.Pq Xr setpriority 2 ,
so that what the console asks for, often, does not crowd the host's
own work; a program run by a job, or for a change asked directly, runs
at the agent's own priority.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
What the agent serves of the models by cblink's YANG family is also
configuration, in RFC 8342's datastores:
.Cm running ,
what is in use, read from the kernel and from what
.Xr rc 8
reads, without what DHCP, SLAAC, the kernel or a routing protocol made;
and
.Cm candidate ,
the configuration being made, shared by every session.
Running changes by a confirmed commit of the candidate alone (RFC 6241
section 8.4): undone at its timeout unless confirmed.
A commit checks the model (types, keys, mandatory nodes,
.Ic when
and
.Ic must )
and NACM's write rules first, then changes, through the handlers, what
it changes, all or nothing.
So far a commit changes:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
FIB 0's static routes, as
.Pa /etc/rc.d/routing
installs them
.Pq Va static_routes , ipv6_static_routes , route_ Ns Ar name ;
.It
an interface's description, whether it is enabled, its IPv4 MTU and
its static addresses, a point-to-point one's with its peer
.Pq Va ifconfig_ Ns Ar if , ifconfig_ Ns Ar if Ns Va _descr ,
.Va ifconfig_ Ns Ar if Ns Va _alias Ns Ar n ;
.It
an interface a cloner makes, made (a gif's or gre's tunnel ends, a
vlan's tag and parent) or destroyed
.Pq Va cloned_interfaces , create_args_ Ns Ar if ;
.It
an interface's router advertisements, RFC 8349's
.Ic ipv6-router-advertisements
with arcana-ra's leaves for the rest of
.Xr rtadvd.conf 5
(the router preference of RFC 4191 and its route information, RFC
8106's RDNSS and DNSSL, RFC 8781's PREF64, mtu=auto, noifprefix,
nolladdr, clockskew, a prefix's vltimedecr and pltimedecr; a field the
agent does not know kept as written in
.Ic other-capability ) :
the interface's record written whole, as one termcap record in the
file's order, the other records and comments untouched;
.Va rtadvd_enable
and
.Va rtadvd_interfaces
where it sends; then
.Xr rtadvctl 8
.Cm reload
of the interface where
.Xr rtadvd 8
runs on the same interfaces as before, else
.Xr rtadvd 8
restarted, or stopped where none is left.
In the operational datastore the node carries
.Ic arcana-ra:rtadvd ,
what rtadvd sends now as
.Xr rtadvctl 8
.Cm show
reports it;
.It
a service's rcvar, YES or NO, and its
.Ar name Ns Va _*
variables (arcana-services), a service at a time; and a jail started at
boot or not, arcana-jails'
.Ic boot
.Pq Va jail_list , jail_enable ;
