anything else is refused as not supported yet.
.Pp
What a commit keeps of
.Xr rc.conf 5
it writes to
.Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.conf.d/arcana ,
which
.Va rc_conf_files
in
.Pa /etc/rc.conf
names, so that
.Xr rc 8
reads it after your files.
Your files are left as they are but for what you accept with the
request: naming the file in
.Va rc_conf_files ,
once
.Pq Cm rc-conf-files ,
and a variable Arcana writes that your files set too, commented out
where it is in yours, the line kept with
.Dq # taken by Arcana
after it
.Pq Cm rc-conf-conflict .
A service's variables are moved under Arcana deliberately by
arcana-services' convert action
.Pq Nm arcanactl Cm services convert ,
which says what it takes, or with dry-run would, by file and line.
Every file is put back where the kernel refuses the change; a route the
table changed meanwhile is tried once more first.
.Pp
Running's ietf-syslog is what
.Xr syslogd 8
reads:
.Pa /etc/syslog.conf
and the files it includes, each file's rotation from
.Pa /etc/newsyslog.conf
and its includes; what the model cannot hold (a pipe, users told, a
block of one program or host, a property filter, a comparison by
.Ql < ,
.Ql >
or
.Ql \&! ,
a rotation at a time of day) is logged and left out.
What a commit writes goes to
.Pa /usr/local/etc/syslog.d/arcana.conf
and its rotations to
.Pa /usr/local/etc/newsyslog.conf.d/arcana.conf ,
each action one line, read where
.Pa /etc/syslog.conf
and
.Pa /etc/newsyslog.conf
include them, as FreeBSD's own do.
An action the commit leaves as it is stays where it is.
Your files are left as they are but for what you accept: their
include of Arcana's file, added once at their end
.Pq Cm syslog-include ,
and a line of yours that writes to an action the commit changes or
takes away, or turns over a log whose rotation it changes, commented
out where it is with
.Dq # taken by Arcana:
.Pq Cm syslog-conf-conflict .
A log file new to syslogd is made, mode 0600, as
.Nm syslogd Fl C
would.
.Xr syslogd 8
has no check of its files of its own: what was written is read back
first, as running is, and must be what was asked; then syslogd, where
it runs, reads them again
.Pq Ql service syslogd onereload ,
and where it does not the commit says so
.Pq Cm syslogd-stopped .
Failing, every file is put back and syslogd told again.
Refused, said: TLS, a destination named otherwise than by its address,
more than one address, a facility override, an advanced compare that
blocks or stops, the facility cron2, a retention, a rollover of other
than whole hours.
.Pp
An undo that fails (a commit not confirmed in time, or cancelled) stops
there, what is left as committed: a Critical alarm
.Pq Cm undo
and an
.Cm undo-failed
event whose report says what failed and why, of the failure alone and
not of the host's configuration, for you to file as a bug if you
choose; Arcana files nothing.
.Sh ITS OWN SERVICE
A stop or restart of
.Nm arcana_agent
asked of the daemon itself, as a service action, is not run and waited
for as other services' are:
.Xr service 8
would wait for the daemon to stop while the daemon waits for it to end.
It is handed to a process of its own, the request is answered, and the
daemon is stopped by that process a moment later.
.Sh STOPPING
On
.Dv SIGTERM
or
.Dv SIGINT ,
as from
.Ql service arcana_agent stop ,
the daemon stops.
A change that is under way is not cut short: the daemon logs what it
is and which jobs wait behind it, starts nothing more, and stops when
the change has ended, reporting again every 30 seconds while it waits.
The jobs that had not started are lost.
A second signal stops it at once, and the log says what was cut short.
A program a change had started keeps running in that case.
.Sh INTERFACES
The network interfaces are read with
.Xr getifaddrs 3
and a few ioctls, as
.Xr ifconfig 8
reads them: flags, link state, MTU, hardware address, description, the
two ends of a tunnel, counters and addresses.
They are changed by jobs that run
.Xr ifconfig 8 :
an address added as an alias or taken off, an interface brought up or
down.
Static routes are added and deleted by jobs that run
.Xr route 8 .
The changes are live only.
.Pp
A job of these kinds may ask for safe mode.
The change is made, and the job waits, in the state
.Li unconfirmed ,
for the client to confirm it; reaching the daemon again is the point.
Without that within the wait
.Pq Fl w , 60 seconds
the daemon undoes the change, as it also does when it is stopped while
waiting, or when the job is cancelled while it waits
.Pq its Li cancel action :
an address is put back with the prefix length it had, an
interface brought back up or down, a route deleted or added again, a
sysctl set to the value it had and its line in
.Pa sysctl.conf
put back or taken out, a route deleted without its gateway added back as
the kernel listed it, a BIRD protocol enabled or disabled again, and
BIRD's configuration taken back by BIRD itself
.Pq Cm configure undo ,
which read it with a timer a little longer than the wait, and is told to
keep it
.Pq Cm configure confirm
when the job is confirmed, and a WireGuard interface synced back
.Pq Cm wg syncconf
from what
.Cm wg showconf
printed before, a text held in memory only and never written to the
trace, with its
.Xr wg-quick 8
file and the
.Pa rc.conf
variables as they were, and an IPsec connection's files put back before
.Xr swanctl 8
reads them again, its SAs ended first when the connection was new, and a
file of the system's written whole put back and its daemon told again,
and a tunnel, tap, tun or loopback interface destroyed made again as it
was read before, a bridge's member, flag, vlanfilter or static address
taken back by the inverse word, a geneve made destroyed again.
What has to be read before the change for that, and cannot be, fails
the job before the change is made.
.Sh BUILDS
A client may ask for
.Nm
to be built from a git repository: the console does when
.Va agent_source
is set, and
.Xr arcanactl 8
with
.Cm agent-build .
The repository is cloned afresh, without history, into the build
directory, and
.Pa lib/libjailconf
and
.Pa usr.sbin/arcana-agent
are built there with
.Xr make 1 .
When the daemon is root, git and make run as
.Li nobody .
For a repository reached over SSH, the server's host key is never
taken on trust: until the client sends back the keys a person
confirmed, the reply carries the keys the server showed and their
fingerprints, and nothing is built.
Confirmed keys are kept in
.Pa known_hosts
in the build directory and checked strictly from then on.
git shows the server a key of this host's, made on first use as
.Pa id_ed25519
there, or the one the client names.
The program is sent back with its SHA-256 and the version it reports,
compressed with gzip when the client asks
.Pq the SHA-256 is still the program's ;
nothing is installed.
One build runs at a time.
.Pp
With
.Cm console-update
the whole tree is built, as the unprivileged user, and installed with
.Ql make install
as the daemon; the
.Nm arcana_console
service is restarted after the reply.
That is how a console updates itself, through the agent of its host.
.Sh UPDATES
A client may send a new
.Nm :
the console does, and
.Xr arcanactl 8
with
.Cm agent-update .
A frame carries at most 6 MiB of it; a client that sees
.Li gzip-update
in
.Ic hello Ns 's
features sends it compressed with gzip
.Pq Xr zlib 3 ,
with the size it inflates to, and the daemon inflates it first: to no
more than that size, nor than 32 MiB, stopping a byte past it.
The program, inflated, is checked against its signature by the
console's CA key (asked of every client but the local socket's) and
the SHA-256 sent with it, written beside
the installed one, and run with
.Fl V ;
one that does not run on this host is dropped.
It then takes the place of the installed program, which is kept with
the suffix
.Pa .old .
When asked to, the daemon has
.Xr service 8
restart
.Nm arcana_agent
after it has replied; jobs still queued are lost, one that is running
ends first.
.Sh RC.CONF VARIABLES
The service
.Nm arcana_agent
always listens on its local socket; network listeners are added to it.
.Bl -tag -width "arcana_agent_listen"
.It Va arcana_agent_enable
Run the agent.
.It Va arcana_agent_socket
The local socket.
Default
.Pa /var/run/arcana-agent.sock .
.It Va arcana_agent_group
A group whose members may use the socket
.Pq Fl g .
Default: none, root only.
.It Va arcana_agent_listen
Network listeners, separated by spaces, such as
.Ql tcp://0.0.0.0:4310 tcp://[::]:4310 .
Default: none.
.It Va arcana_agent_ca , arcana_agent_cert , arcana_agent_key
The files for
.Fl A ,
.Fl C
and
.Fl K ,
used when there are network listeners.
Default:
.Pa ca.pem ,
.Pa host.pem
and
.Pa host.key
in
.Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana .
.It Va arcana_agent_flags
More flags, added to those the variables above give.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /var/run/arcana-agent.sock
.It Pa /var/run/arcana-agent.pid
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Serve the console host over TLS and local tools over the default
socket:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# arcana-agent -A /usr/local/etc/arcana/ca.pem \e
    -C /usr/local/etc/arcana/host.pem \e
    -K /usr/local/etc/arcana/host.key \e
    -l unix:/var/run/arcana-agent.sock \e
    -l tcp://0.0.0.0:4310 -l 'tcp://[::]:4310'
.Ed
